      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We used lornoxicam (n = 16) and ketorolac (n = 20) to study the possibilities of applying the non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs within the postoperative patient-controllable analgesia (PCA). With respect to a used analgetic, the frequency rate of good PCA anesthetic results was found, on day 1, to be 60-77%. The good anesthetic results were registered in 25% of patients when the routine scheme was in use. Non-steroid anti-inflammatory agents (lornoxicam, ketorolac) can be prescribed within the early postoperative PCA as basic analgetics, which essentially reduces the need in promedol without worsening the analgesia efficiency."},
